-- title:
--   Saturation of the geometric special fibre components of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and the intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the field generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image, under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= q^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{num}}$. Write $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), the structure morphism of the model obtained as the pushout glueing the spectra of the $A$-subalgebras of $K$ generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with an $A$-algebra structure, and put $X_k = X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} k$. Let $C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $i_1, i_2$ be closed immersions of $C_1, C_2$ into $X_k$ commuting with the projections to $\operatorname{Spec} k$, such that every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$. The conclusion is that for all points $x, x'$ of $X_k$ having the same image under the projection $X_k \to X$, one has $x \in \operatorname{im} i_1 \iff x' \in \operatorname{im} i_1$, and likewise $x \in \operatorname{im} i_2 \iff x' \in \operatorname{im} i_2$.
--
--   This expresses that each of the two curves covering the geometric special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$ is saturated for the projection to the model over $A$, equivalently that the two irreducible components of the special fibre over the residue field — the Igusa component and its Atkin–Lehner twist — remain irreducible after passing to an algebraically closed field. It is used in the analysis of the minimal primes and of the images of the two components in the special fibre, in the description of the reduction of $X_1(Mp)$ underlying the level-lowering argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_mem_range_iff_mem_range_of_fst_eq_specialFibre_components_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

